{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790710043,"nonce":"eZise6KQxxFgnxd3t2WvdsDmOVg=","message":"Fixed by ad4560e683ce0893a144bd5808209b85466fbfb3 (Defer the default string metatable).\n\n`zl_meta_of` now reads an already-installed string metatable instead of calling `zl_string_metatable`. String indexing supplies the default `__index` behavior directly, so unrelated metamethod probes no longer make the string library reachable.\n\nReachability on any_field falls from 355 to 271 kept functions. On the x86_64 NUC with the LLVM backend enabled, lowering falls from 10.99 ms to 9.05 ms. In 21 interleaved NUC runs, median wall time falls from 36.622 ms to 34.165 ms (6.7%); LuaJIT is 2.218 ms. Median kernel times are 1.733 ms before, 1.868 ms after, and 0.966 ms for LuaJIT; all produce result 1500000.\n\nOn the Mac, 21 interleaved runs move wall time from 27.131 ms to 25.302 ms (6.7%); LuaJIT is 4.901 ms. The compiled loop remains folded, at 0.046 ms after the change.\n\nValidated metatables, strings, and debug conformance in normal and warm-up modes with no regressions (92 case executions total).","files":null}]}